body:
@katre My understanding of platform mappings was that this is a temporary mechanism that will go away once the platforms approach is mature enough. I've created the issue not because I need this solved here and now, but rather because I thought this needs to be solved eventually. I'm working in a project that effectively has implemented something close to the platforms approach internally, just using the `--cpu` flag as a selector.
We have a bunch of common libraries that target Intel, ARM and PowerPC platforms and it is a great convenience to have the binary artifacts for different platforms be automatically separated out instead of being overwritten with each recompilation.
For now we've simply put the migration off until platforms get more mature, but in that mature solution it'd be good to have this addressed in some way.
